# Empty on purpose: `npm run dev` proxies /api/* to the local backend (see
# the `server.proxy` block in vite.config.ts), so the frontend and the API
# look like the same origin to the browser — same reason production goes
# through the Cloudflare Worker (frontend/worker/) instead of hitting Render
# directly. This is what makes the httpOnly refresh-token cookie work in
# local dev too. If you want the SPA to call the backend directly instead
# (bypassing the proxy), set this to http://127.0.0.1:8000 — but then
# refresh-on-reload won't work, since the cookie won't be sent cross-origin.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
